From 017558e9b1d80daeac719740937affbc8e7b6821 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Athappilly <jamesatha@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:27:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add option to disable password authentication

This introduces the password-auth build option which toggles password
based auth. This is enabled by default to keep the existing behavior.
This enforces the requirement at the shared PAM authentication
entrypoint to reject Basic, web UI, and Redfish password logins.

When bmcweb is upgraded with password auth disabled, when existing
cookies or tokens are used, they will be revoked when used.
This also disallows PATCH requests from re-enabling Basic
authentication.

Signed-off-by: James Athappilly <jamesatha@gmail.com>
Change-Id: Ic0622b28e9f0e4398f830563b55d10659458931c
